1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:05,274
Lesson 4.3: Updating Clinical Data. Part 2:

2
00:00:05,314 --> 00:00:09,242
Lab Results, Medications, and Immunizations.

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,864
In part one, you updated Conditions and Allergies.

4
00:00:13,904 --> 00:00:17,086
This part covers the last three sections.

5
00:00:17,136 --> 00:00:18,214
In Lab Results,

6
00:00:18,254 --> 00:00:23,514
you add the latest result of every lab the patient's CCM conditions need.

7
00:00:23,564 --> 00:00:28,248
In Medications, you add the patient's whole medication list from PointClickCare,

8
00:00:28,288 --> 00:00:30,080
and reconcile it.

9
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:35,236
In Immunizations, you add every vaccine the patient has had, or refused.

10
00:00:35,286 --> 00:00:38,327
Each section must match PointClickCare exactly.

11
00:00:39,568 --> 00:00:44,204
Back in ThoroughCare, on the Clinical Data tab, open Lab Results.

12
00:00:45,067 --> 00:00:50,529
Lab Results lists the patient's lab results. For this patient, it's still empty.

13
00:00:50,579 --> 00:00:55,521
Here, you add the labs that monitor each of the patient's CCM conditions.

14
00:00:55,571 --> 00:01:01,133
Which labs to add comes from the monitoring criteria in the Update Care Policy.

15
00:01:03,933 --> 00:01:08,309
Open the Update Care Policy. It holds the guidelines you work from.

16
00:01:08,367 --> 00:01:13,304
It sets what you monitor for every condition that you manage under CCM.

17
00:01:19,167 --> 00:01:21,298
Go to the Numbers to Track tab.

18
00:01:22,933 --> 00:01:27,275
For each condition, it lists the labs and vital signs to monitor.

19
00:01:28,233 --> 00:01:32,563
For example, this patient's CCM condition is hypertension.

20
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:37,393
For hypertension, you track hemoglobin and hematocrit,

21
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:42,324
kidney function: BUN, creatinine, and GFR,

22
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:48,517
the lipid panel: total cholesterol, LDL, HDL, and triglycerides,

23
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:51,351
hemoglobin A1C, and TSH.

24
00:01:51,401 --> 00:01:53,002
Blood pressure is on the list too,

25
00:01:53,042 --> 00:01:57,161
but it's a vital sign, so it isn't added in Lab Results.

26
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:03,820
Note that hemoglobin A1C is tracked for every patient you follow,

27
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:05,738
whatever their condition.

28
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:09,798
For each of these labs, you find its latest result in PointClickCare,

29
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:12,108
and add it in ThoroughCare.

30
00:02:13,933 --> 00:02:17,040
Now open the patient's record in PointClickCare.

31
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:20,416
Search for the patient by name, and open their record.

32
00:02:25,107 --> 00:02:26,828
Open the Results tab.

33
00:02:26,878 --> 00:02:31,129
It lists every lab report for the patient, with the newest at the top.

34
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:35,558
Start with hemoglobin and hematocrit.

35
00:02:35,598 --> 00:02:39,715
They're part of the complete blood count, or CBC.

36
00:02:40,667 --> 00:02:43,815
The newest report with a CBC is at the top.

37
00:02:45,467 --> 00:02:49,624
Its collection date is October 5, 2026.

38
00:02:53,023 --> 00:02:56,363
To open it, click Actions, and then View Results.

39
00:02:56,413 --> 00:02:58,993
The lab report opens in a new window.

40
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:07,661
Under CBC w/Auto Diff, find hemoglobin: 10.5 grams per deciliter.

41
00:03:07,711 --> 00:03:11,040
Then hematocrit: 33.3 percent.

42
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:14,130
Both results were collected on October 5,

43
00:03:14,170 --> 00:03:18,488
2026. Now you add them in ThoroughCare.

44
00:03:22,967 --> 00:03:26,436
To add a lab in ThoroughCare, you need its LOINC code.

45
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,990
LOINC codes are standard codes for lab tests,

46
00:03:30,030 --> 00:03:34,380
the way ICD-10 codes identify diagnoses.

47
00:03:34,433 --> 00:03:39,147
The Numbers to Track tab lists each lab's code, in the Loinc Code column.

48
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:43,410
Hemoglobin's code is 718-7. Copy it.

49
00:03:47,745 --> 00:03:50,605
Back in ThoroughCare, click New Lab Result.

50
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:53,318
The Add/Edit Lab window opens.

51
00:03:53,368 --> 00:03:56,224
In Lab Result (LOINC Code), paste the code,

52
00:03:56,274 --> 00:04:01,352
and select 718-7 | Hemoglobin [Mass/volume] in Blood.

53
00:04:01,402 --> 00:04:04,481
In Value, type the result: 10.5.

54
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:11,118
In Recorded At, enter the collection date: 10/05/2026.

55
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,971
Set Status to Completed.

56
00:04:13,933 --> 00:04:18,115
Status is always Completed, because the lab has already been done.

57
00:04:18,167 --> 00:04:22,703
Abnormal Flag shows whether the value is outside the normal range.

58
00:04:24,333 --> 00:04:26,467
To check, go back to the report.

59
00:04:28,667 --> 00:04:35,696
Hemoglobin is 10.5, and its reference range is 13.7 to 17.5.

60
00:04:35,746 --> 00:04:39,715
10.5 is below that range, so the result is low.

61
00:04:40,667 --> 00:04:43,807
Back in the lab window, open Abnormal Flag,

62
00:04:44,569 --> 00:04:46,614
and choose L - Below low normal.

63
00:04:46,900 --> 00:04:50,401
If a result is above the range, choose H - Above high normal.

64
00:04:50,441 --> 00:04:54,711
If it's within the range, leave Abnormal Flag empty.

65
00:04:54,775 --> 00:04:56,141
Then click Save.

66
00:04:56,467 --> 00:04:59,593
The result is saved: hemoglobin, 10.5,

67
00:04:59,633 --> 00:05:04,754
below low normal, October 5, 2026, Completed.

68
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:10,104
Repeat these steps for every lab on the list for the patient's conditions.

69
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,956
For hypertension, that's hematocrit,

70
00:05:13,996 --> 00:05:18,123
kidney function, the lipid panel, A1C, and TSH.

71
00:05:19,067 --> 00:05:23,040
For each lab, add only its latest result from the last year.

72
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:26,674
If a lab has no result from the last year, don't add it.

73
00:05:26,733 --> 00:05:30,898
For example, if this patient had no TSH result in the last year,

74
00:05:30,939 --> 00:05:32,988
you would skip TSH.

75
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:39,684
Keep going until every lab for the patient's conditions is in Lab Results.

76
00:05:42,437 --> 00:05:44,520
Next, open Medications.

77
00:05:45,633 --> 00:05:48,207
Here, you add the patient's whole medication list,

78
00:05:48,247 --> 00:05:51,347
exactly as it is in PointClickCare.

79
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:56,734
That's every medication the patient takes now, not only their CCM medications.

80
00:05:56,800 --> 00:06:01,507
If you added medications in the initial assessment, they're already listed here.

81
00:06:03,604 --> 00:06:07,484
If nothing is missing, just click Reconcile Medications.

82
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:12,874
A message confirms the medications are reconciled, and the date is recorded.

83
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:17,778
If a medication is missing, find it in PointClickCare.

84
00:06:18,741 --> 00:06:20,425
Open the Orders tab.

85
00:06:21,386 --> 00:06:24,785
First, filter the orders. Click Display Filters.

86
00:06:24,835 --> 00:06:27,814
Under Order Category, keep only Pharmacy checked,

87
00:06:27,854 --> 00:06:29,894
and clear the other categories.

88
00:06:30,875 --> 00:06:32,280
Then click Search.

89
00:06:32,333 --> 00:06:36,758
Now the list shows only pharmacy orders: the patient's medications.

90
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:45,010
For example, the patient takes Eliquis Oral Tablet 5 MG (Apixaban).

91
00:06:45,067 --> 00:06:46,411
Copy its name,

92
00:06:47,067 --> 00:06:51,019
and its full directions: give 1 tablet by mouth two times a day,

93
00:06:51,059 --> 00:06:54,950
related to unspecified atrial fibrillation.

94
00:06:55,902 --> 00:06:58,503
In ThoroughCare, click New Medication.

95
00:06:58,567 --> 00:07:01,633
The Add/Edit Medication window opens.

96
00:07:01,683 --> 00:07:03,706
Paste the directions in Notes.

97
00:07:03,767 --> 00:07:08,101
In Medication, press Windows key + V to open your clipboard history,

98
00:07:08,141 --> 00:07:09,764
and paste the name.

99
00:07:09,814 --> 00:07:14,321
Then click Create "Eliquis Oral Tablet 5 MG (Apixaban)",

100
00:07:14,361 --> 00:07:18,586
so the name is exactly as it is in PointClickCare.

101
00:07:19,533 --> 00:07:21,622
Fill in the rest from the directions.

102
00:07:22,567 --> 00:07:24,522
Dosage: 1 tablet.

103
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:27,575
Frequency: twice a day.

104
00:07:28,533 --> 00:07:31,249
Route: oral, because it's taken by mouth.

105
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:36,480
Reason Taken: atrial fibrillation, as the directions say.

106
00:07:36,842 --> 00:07:38,207
Then click Save.

107
00:07:38,433 --> 00:07:43,551
Eliquis is now in the list, with its dosage, frequency, route, and reason.

108
00:07:44,400 --> 00:07:47,223
Repeat this for every medication in PointClickCare:

109
00:07:47,263 --> 00:07:51,480
the whole list, not only the CCM medications.

110
00:07:53,059 --> 00:07:57,384
When the list matches PointClickCare, click Reconcile Medications.

111
00:07:57,434 --> 00:08:01,825
This confirms that you reviewed the medication list, and that it's up to date.

112
00:08:04,535 --> 00:08:08,444
The last section to update is Immunizations. Open it.

113
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:13,388
Here, you add every vaccine the patient has had: the whole list.

114
00:08:13,438 --> 00:08:17,344
You take the list from PointClickCare, and follow a few rules.

115
00:08:23,816 --> 00:08:26,663
In PointClickCare, open the IMMUN tab.

116
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:30,957
It lists every immunization the patient has had,

117
00:08:30,997 --> 00:08:34,493
with its CVX code, date, and status.

118
00:08:35,433 --> 00:08:37,572
Here are the rules for ThoroughCare.

119
00:08:37,633 --> 00:08:40,964
First, for COVID-19 and influenza vaccines,

120
00:08:41,004 --> 00:08:45,051
always choose the unspecified vaccine in ThoroughCare.

121
00:08:46,167 --> 00:08:51,166
Second, add every vaccine that was completed, historical, or refused.

122
00:08:52,300 --> 00:08:55,244
Don't add a vaccine that's still pending confirmation,

123
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:57,832
or one the patient hasn't had yet.

124
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:02,568
Third, a TB skin test isn't a vaccine.

125
00:09:03,533 --> 00:09:08,129
The TB 2 Step Mantoux Skin Test is a skin test for tuberculosis,

126
00:09:08,169 --> 00:09:12,120
also called a PPD test, so you don't add it.

127
00:09:13,067 --> 00:09:16,072
Now add the vaccines, starting with COVID-19.

128
00:09:16,112 --> 00:09:21,258
The patient received it on December 21, 2022.

129
00:09:23,002 --> 00:09:25,748
In ThoroughCare, click New Immunization.

130
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:29,066
The Add/Edit Immunization window opens.

131
00:09:29,123 --> 00:09:32,687
In Immunization, type the vaccine's name: covid.

132
00:09:34,788 --> 00:09:39,277
Choose SARS-COV-2 (COVID-19) vaccine, UNSPECIFIED.

133
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:42,951
Set Status to Completed, because the vaccine was given.

134
00:09:43,001 --> 00:09:46,768
Set Route to Intramuscular. Always choose Intramuscular.

135
00:09:47,733 --> 00:09:54,300
For Date, use the date administered in PointClickCare: 12/21/2022.

136
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:56,960
Type it in the Date field.

137
00:09:57,010 --> 00:09:58,375
Then click Save.

138
00:09:58,433 --> 00:10:03,847
The COVID-19 vaccine is added, with its date, Completed, and Intramuscular.

139
00:10:05,133 --> 00:10:10,029
Repeat these steps for every vaccine on the list. Next, influenza.

140
00:10:10,079 --> 00:10:15,209
Patients get an influenza vaccine every year, so there can be several doses.

141
00:10:16,167 --> 00:10:20,842
You don't add every dose. You add only the latest one, if it was completed.

142
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:24,875
If the latest dose was refused, add that refusal,

143
00:10:24,915 --> 00:10:28,059
and also the last dose that was completed.

144
00:10:28,109 --> 00:10:34,390
Here, the latest dose is October 13, 2026, and its status is Complete.

145
00:10:36,067 --> 00:10:41,336
So you add only that one, not the dose from November 3, 2025.

146
00:10:42,302 --> 00:10:45,048
In ThoroughCare, click New Immunization.

147
00:10:45,100 --> 00:10:46,476
Search for flu.

148
00:10:48,055 --> 00:10:52,609
Choose influenza virus vaccine, unspecified formulation.

149
00:10:52,667 --> 00:10:53,803
Always choose this one,

150
00:10:53,843 --> 00:10:58,224
whatever the influenza vaccine is called in PointClickCare.

151
00:10:58,274 --> 00:11:01,825
Set Status to Completed, and Route to Intramuscular.

152
00:11:01,875 --> 00:11:07,794
For Date, use the date from PointClickCare: 10/13/2026.

153
00:11:07,867 --> 00:11:12,634
The date typed in this recording is 10/21/2026,

154
00:11:12,674 --> 00:11:16,668
which doesn't match. Always copy the date exactly.

155
00:11:16,718 --> 00:11:18,083
Then click Save.

156
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:20,696
The influenza vaccine is added.

157
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:23,823
Next is PREVNAR.

158
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:27,646
If you don't recognize a vaccine's name, search for it online.

159
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:31,154
PREVNAR is a pneumococcal vaccine.

160
00:11:32,102 --> 00:11:34,848
In ThoroughCare, click New Immunization.

161
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:36,086
Type pneumo.

162
00:11:37,733 --> 00:11:40,387
Pneumococcal vaccines come in several types,

163
00:11:40,427 --> 00:11:46,277
by valence: 7, 10, 13, 15, 20, or 23-valent.

164
00:11:49,533 --> 00:11:52,925
PointClickCare doesn't say which type this patient had.

165
00:11:54,905 --> 00:11:59,034
So choose pneumococcal vaccine, unspecified formulation.

166
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:02,650
Set Status to Completed, and Route to Intramuscular.

167
00:12:03,767 --> 00:12:09,395
For Date, use the date from PointClickCare: 01/03/2023.

168
00:12:09,445 --> 00:12:11,737
Here too, the recording shows a different date,

169
00:12:11,777 --> 00:12:17,529
10/12/2026. Always use the PointClickCare date.

170
00:12:17,579 --> 00:12:18,945
Then click Save.

171
00:12:19,267 --> 00:12:21,525
The pneumococcal vaccine is added.

172
00:12:23,267 --> 00:12:28,413
If PointClickCare names the exact vaccine, choose the matching option instead.

173
00:12:29,533 --> 00:12:36,118
For example, if it says Prevnar 20, choose Pneumococcal Vaccine: PCV20 Vaccine.

174
00:12:37,233 --> 00:12:42,112
Choose an unspecified vaccine only when PointClickCare doesn't specify it,

175
00:12:42,152 --> 00:12:45,997
and always for COVID-19 and influenza.

176
00:12:46,958 --> 00:12:49,970
Here, PREVNAR isn't specified, so cancel.

177
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:53,574
What if the patient refused a vaccine?

178
00:12:55,767 --> 00:12:58,943
Suppose the patient refused the COVID-19 vaccine.

179
00:12:58,983 --> 00:13:01,650
Here's how you would document it.

180
00:13:07,567 --> 00:13:13,571
Follow the same steps: choose SARS-COV-2 (COVID-19) vaccine, UNSPECIFIED,

181
00:13:13,621 --> 00:13:16,089
but set Status to Patient Refused.

182
00:13:17,233 --> 00:13:19,262
Route is still Intramuscular.

183
00:13:20,200 --> 00:13:22,928
A refused vaccine needs one extra step:

184
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:25,826
a note in Notes, written from a template.

185
00:13:27,133 --> 00:13:30,158
The template is in the CCM Clinical Tool.

186
00:13:31,267 --> 00:13:34,891
Open its Templates tab. It has every template you need.

187
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:40,869
Under Immunization, find Refused vaccine.

188
00:13:40,933 --> 00:13:41,592
It says:

189
00:13:41,632 --> 00:13:47,915
Patient has not received (name of vaccine) vaccine and declined administration at this time.

190
00:13:48,867 --> 00:13:49,912
Copy it.

191
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:52,589
Paste it in Notes.

192
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:59,255
Replace (name of vaccine) with the vaccine's name from PointClickCare: COVID-19.

193
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:04,762
Then add the date of the refusal.

194
00:14:07,933 --> 00:14:13,193
For a refused vaccine, the Date Administered column in PointClickCare is blank.

195
00:14:14,133 --> 00:14:15,132
To find the date,

196
00:14:15,172 --> 00:14:19,300
click the three dots at the end of the vaccine's row, and then View.

197
00:14:20,233 --> 00:14:22,341
View Immunization shows the details.

198
00:14:22,381 --> 00:14:25,911
For a refused vaccine, take the date from here.

199
00:14:26,779 --> 00:14:28,906
Back in ThoroughCare, click Save.

200
00:14:29,867 --> 00:14:33,496
The vaccine is saved with Patient Refused, and the note.

201
00:14:34,433 --> 00:14:37,007
Remember, this refusal was only an example.

202
00:14:37,047 --> 00:14:40,687
This patient's COVID-19 vaccine was given,

203
00:14:40,737 --> 00:14:45,458
so in real work, it stays Completed, with its date from PointClickCare.

204
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:51,214
To sum up, document every vaccine that was completed or refused.

205
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:54,489
For influenza, add the latest dose if it was completed.

206
00:14:54,529 --> 00:14:58,760
If it was refused, add it and the last completed dose.

207
00:14:58,810 --> 00:15:03,819
And for COVID-19 and influenza, always choose the unspecified vaccine,

208
00:15:03,859 --> 00:15:06,933
even if PointClickCare names the brand,

209
00:15:06,983 --> 00:15:10,422
for example, Pfizer, Moderna, or AstraZeneca.

210
00:15:14,233 --> 00:15:18,622
When Immunizations is done, the patient's clinical data is complete.

211
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,393
Let's recap.

212
00:15:22,443 --> 00:15:27,227
In Lab Results, check Numbers to Track for the labs each condition needs.

213
00:15:27,277 --> 00:15:30,038
Find each lab's latest result from the last year,

214
00:15:30,078 --> 00:15:32,702
in PointClickCare's Results tab.

215
00:15:32,752 --> 00:15:34,822
Add it with its LOINC code, the value,

216
00:15:34,862 --> 00:15:37,920
the date, Completed, and the Abnormal Flag.

217
00:15:37,970 --> 00:15:41,680
In Medications, filter PointClickCare's orders to Pharmacy,

218
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:45,035
and add every medication with its details.

219
00:15:45,085 --> 00:15:47,528
Then click Reconcile Medications.

220
00:15:47,578 --> 00:15:53,020
In Immunizations, add every vaccine from the IMMUN tab, but not skin tests.

221
00:15:53,070 --> 00:15:57,402
Choose the unspecified vaccine for COVID-19 and influenza,

222
00:15:57,442 --> 00:16:01,426
and when PointClickCare doesn't name the exact vaccine.

223
00:16:01,476 --> 00:16:07,202
For a refused vaccine, set Status to Patient Refused, and add the refusal note.

224
00:16:09,367 --> 00:16:12,809
That's part two, and the end of lesson 4.3.

225
00:16:12,859 --> 00:16:15,172
The patient's lab results, medications,

226
00:16:15,212 --> 00:16:18,656
and immunizations now match PointClickCare.
